From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Maria Blasco <josep.maria.blasco@epbcn.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 11:46:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/13] WebAssembly port, Node: external commands, host paths,
 signals

wasm/build-node.sh relinks the runtime (no recompilation) as a Node-only
command-line ooRexx that sees the host file system and environment
(NODERAWFS, wasm/node-pre.js), with rexx and rexxc launchers.

- ADDRESS commands under Node run as host processes (child_process.spawnSync
  on the interpreter thread), with ADDRESS ... WITH redirection: the host
  functions orxWasmCommandRun() and friends (SysWasmHost.hpp); in the
  browser they still fail closed;
- .RexxInfo~executable and ~libraryPath from the location of rexx.js (the
  host functions orxWasmExecutablePath() and orxWasmLibraryDirectory());
- the class files installed in the build;
- LINES() / CHARS() on the host's stdin: SysFile::hasData() asks
  ioctl(FIONREAD), which Emscripten answers 0 without writing the count;
  node-pre.js answers it (a file: the bytes left; a terminal, /dev/null:
  0; a pipe: read ahead), the same results as native;
- SIGINT (Ctrl-C), SIGTERM and SIGHUP raise HALT in the running program,
  as natively, instead of ending the Node process: node-pre.js calls
  orxWasmSignal();
- samples/rexxtry.rex copied next to rexx (`rexx rexxtry`);
- wasm/tests/qualify-node-cli.sh: qualification of the Node command-line
  build, with assertions.
